            "<p>Have properties of both metals and non-metals</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2hlt8ew",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Periodic Trends"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v54d04k",
      "content": "• Atomic size decreases across a period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4p4mt0h",
      "content": "• Atomic size increases down a group."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "umdg007",
      "content": "• Metallic character decreases across a period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gil0mpm",
      "content": "• Electronegativity increases across a period."
    },
    {
      "id": "isjaqsb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Importance of Periodic Table"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j2yp8xc",
      "content": "• Helps understand properties of elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Mendeleev's Periodic Table was arranged by Atomic Mass, while Moseley's Modern Periodic Table is arranged by Atomic Number.",
        "Newlands' Law of Octaves was applicable only up to Calcium.",
        "Atomic radius decreases across a period from left to right and increases down a group in the Modern Periodic Table."
      ],
      "id": "762xb0i"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0w4458v",
      "content": "• Predicts properties of undiscovered elements."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cbc2sxi",
      "content": "• Helps classify elements into groups."
    },
    {
      "id": "7iptldl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h6vbft5",
      "content": "• Mendeleev is called the Father of Periodic Table."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sivnbm7",
      "content": "• Modern periodic table is based on atomic number."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bscag6e",
      "content": "• There are 7 periods and 18 groups."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g7r32jb",
      "content": "• Noble gases belong to group 18."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}